   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">21855</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:rights>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">FAO. Editorial use only. Photo credit must be given.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Vegetation in the River Chota valley. - - Special Programme for Food Security Fruit and Vegetable Processing: ECU/98/30. The aim of this Special Programme for Food Security is to improve the level of a poor Afro-Ecuadorian community in the dry rural valleys of Ecuador, through the establishment of a micro-enterprise for fruit and vegetable conservation and processing, which will generate job opportunities, reduce post-harvest losses and make available safe processed fruit and vegetable products.&#xA;&#xA;A women's group in the area, which has benefited from the project has taken the initiative to undertake productive projects to improve their precarious situation and they are now producing guava jam.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <xmpMM:DerivedFrom rdf:parseType="Resource"/>
